step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test the best single model hypothesis by evaluating CWT_catboost alone.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"CWT_catboost"}

Thought: Test trimmed_mean over the full pool with 20% trimming to see if expanding the pool improves robustness.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the most stable pool (pool1) to see if it improves over trimmed mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a robust median over the slightly larger pool2 to see if adding the extra model improves the already best median pool1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Test a deterministic Bayesian averaging (dba) on the stable pool1 to see if it improves over the median winner.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a robust median on the largest stable pool (pool3) to see if expanding the pool improves over median pool1.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool3"}

Thought: Test a weighted average using inverse_error on the most stable pool (pool1) to see if a data‑driven weighting beats the robust median.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","models":["DWT_rf","FT_rf","CWT_catboost","DWT_catboost","FT_catboost"],"weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean combination on the smaller pool4 to see if expanding the pool size improves over median pool1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Evaluate a robust dba combination on the largest stable pool (pool3) to see if it can beat the median pool1 leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool3","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a trimmed‑mean combination on the smaller pool4 to see if trimming improves over the mean or median on that pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool4","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a different best_single hypothesis by using FT_catboost, which is a strong seasonal model.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"FT_catboost"}

Thought: Evaluate a robust median combination on the smallest pool to see if it improves over the current trimmed_mean winner.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4"}

